# Sandswirl Wanderglyph: "Whenever an opponent casts a spell during their turn, they can't attack you or planeswalkers you
# control this turn. Each opponent who attacked you or a planeswalker you control this turn can't cast spells." The planeswalker
# half of both sentences, with three players so the barred creature still has a player to attack (Bot3) and is asked to declare.
# Turn one: Bot1 casts Wrenn and Six and Unstable Glyphbridge; turn four it crafts the Glyphbridge with the Black Lotus in its
# graveyard. Turn five: Bot2's Lightning Bolt lays the rule on its Savannah Lions, which can attack neither Bot1 nor Wrenn and Six
# (CR 508.1c) but may attack Bot3. Turn eight: nothing was cast, so the Lions attack Wrenn and Six (its defending player is Bot1,
# CR 506.2), and Bot2, having attacked a planeswalker Bot1 controls, cannot cast its second Lightning Bolt.

